-- DC22 - ReservoirCalc Pro PROFESSIONAL (intermediate tier) goes deep.
--
-- Flips (reservoircalc, intermediate) onto the DC1 deep path by inserting its
-- ACTIVE academy_course_structures row, generated from the repo manifest
-- src/content/courses/reservoircalc/intermediate/manifest.json (the structure
-- source of truth; emitted by a generator, not hand-typed), and seeding the six
-- module quiz banks plus the final exam. Answer keys live only here and in the
-- table.
--
-- Every numeric item traces to the reservoircalc teaching oracle and reproduces
-- the live NG6 Professional capstone answer key: a sealing fault at an easting
-- of 1800 m splits the Ekene accumulation at the 1560 m contact into a west
-- block of 117 cells, 18.079852294921874e6 m3 of gross rock and 9.85561714769438
-- MMstb, and an east block of 52 cells, 4.189183349609375e6 m3 and
-- 2.2835909598023787 MMstb. Both cell counts are graded exactly. The same
-- pipeline src/lib/reservoircalcTeaching.js drives and blockLab.test.js pins, on
-- the shared @petrolord/engines gridding and earthmodeling engines.
--
-- Tier note: the Associate tier (DC9) owns the map, the contact, the oil column
-- and the volumetric chain, and its field booking of 169 cells,
-- 22.26903564453125e6 m3 and 12.139208107496763 MMstb appears here only as the
-- check a partition is measured against. This tier owns the partition: the label
-- per node and the separate accumulator per label; the fault landing exactly on
-- node column 14 and the strict inequality that sends that whole column east,
-- worth 0.901423070198863 MMstb on a tie break; the term-by-term additivity of
-- the chain (cells, gross rock volume and net volume add bit for bit, pore
-- volume, HCPV and STOIIP differ by about 5e-15 because zoneVolumes accumulates
-- "total" in its own register); area against barrels, 69.2 pct of the cells
-- carrying 81.2 pct of the oil because the west mean column is 15.452865209334936
-- m against 8.056121826171875 m; the map's ignorance of the fault, which is worth
-- 1.98988907518721 MMstb on the west block when the single eastern well that
-- found oil is removed from the control; and two blocks with two contacts, where
-- the east block runs from 18 cells and 0.3278594720205908 MMstb at 1550 m to 73
-- cells and 5.810976711955219 MMstb at 1570 m.
--
-- Bank standard: measured on the length RANK of the correct option and checked
-- for cyclic key sequences, answer-index skew and within-pool near-duplicates
-- before seeding. Across the 132 questions the correct option is longest in 23
-- pct and shortest in 23 pct, so neither "pick the longest" nor "pick the
-- shortest" beats the 25 pct a guess would score.
--
-- Enrollment grandfathering: enforced_from defaults to now() on first insert, so
-- learners enrolled before this apply finish on the old path; the ON CONFLICT
-- update deliberately leaves enforced_from unchanged on re-seeds. Re-seeding
-- replaces the whole bank for this course-tier; fine while there are no open
-- attempts (open attempts pin question ids).
--
-- Ladder note: an INTERMEDIATE enrollment needs an unrevoked ASSOCIATE
-- certification on the SAME app, so the dry-run probes back-stop a reservoircalc
-- associate cert in-transaction, and a probe confirms the tier below
-- (reservoircalc beginner) is left undisturbed at 132 questions.
--
-- NO DDL. Data only.
-- ============================================================================

